WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
I spent three months in Japan.

00:00:01.141 --> 00:00:04.221
No one ever came up to me and just randomly talk to me.

00:00:04.222 --> 00:00:07.241
But literally the first day I came to Busan,

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.700
like I had a girl like help me with my luggage.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:10.621
I didn't even ask her.

00:00:10.622 --> 00:00:14.381
She just came in like Batman and help them save the day.

00:00:14.382 --> 00:00:16.501
I'll be standing in the metro with my brother

00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:17.781
and I'll have some people,

00:00:17.782 --> 00:00:19.101
oh, where are you from?

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:20.621
You're from Canada. That's so cool.

00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:22.501
I have someone that lives in Vancouver.

00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:23.421
So I, it's just more,

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:24.581
it feels more welcoming here,

00:00:24.582 --> 00:00:26.681
more warm. I feel like there's a,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.860
it's like coldness in Japan that you feel.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.501
I'm not saying Japanese people aren't nice.

00:00:30.502 --> 00:00:32.301
That's absolutely not what I'm saying at all.

00:00:32.302 --> 00:00:35.221
But I just feel like they will take initiative to come

00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:37.593
and maybe talk to you a bit more in my experience.
